1. Definitions

“Dopad” means the project and materials covered by this license.

“Official Release” means an unmodified application package published by the Dopad maintainers through the official Dopad release page at https://github.com/duongonix/dopad/releases.

“Forked Build” means an application or package built from a fork, copy, or modified version of Dopad source code outside the official release process.

“Commercial Purpose” means an activity primarily intended for commercial advantage or monetary compensation. This includes selling or licensing a Forked Build for a fee, bundling it with a paid product, offering it through a paid service, or deploying it in the ordinary operations of a for-profit business.

2. Permission to Use and Modify

You may access, study, copy, modify, build, run, and share Dopad source code and Forked Builds for non-commercial purposes, provided you comply with this license.

You may download, install, run, and redistribute an unmodified Official Release for any purpose, including commercial use, provided that you do not modify it or present it as your own product.

3. Commercial Fork Restriction

Without prior written permission from the Dopad maintainers, you may not build, use, sell, license, distribute, bundle, host, or otherwise offer a Forked Build for a Commercial Purpose.

This restriction applies to internal business deployment as well as public or paid distribution. A separate written commercial license is required for commercial use of a Forked Build.

4. Notices and Modified Builds

Keep this license and all applicable copyright and attribution notices with copies of Dopad or a Forked Build.

Clearly identify a Forked Build as modified and do not state or imply that it is an official Dopad release.

